{"id": 19540, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 10-day-old boy born at home is brought to the emergency department due to difficulty breathing and sweating with feeds.\u00a0 He was born at 38 weeks gestation via spontaneous vaginal delivery.\u00a0 The patient has been breastfeeding every 2 hours for 5-10 minutes per side.\u00a0 The mother notes that he sweats and his lips turn blue while he feeds.\u00a0 Weight is at the 5th percentile and length is at the 50th percentile.\u00a0 On examination, the patient is currently not cyanotic.\u00a0 There is a III/VI systolic crescendo-decrescendo murmur best heard along the left upper sternal border.\u00a0 Chest x-ray is shown below:</p><div class=\"mb-4 text-start flex justify-start items-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"w-full\"><button class=\"lg:max-w-lg md:max-w-md w-fit max-w-full my-5 hover:scale-[1.01] transition-[transform,_box-shadow] ease-in-out duration-500 hover:shadow-lg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-none\" src=\"../../Assets/images/qabzz1kbp7op52p3vs90d6ur.jpg\"/></button></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Which of the following pressure changes most likely occur in this patient during feedings?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u20